+
+### L-second-fort-cupola-2388 — A capped drum on the second fort's blockhouse
+
+**Covers:** `fort_dearborn_blockhouse.log_1816.form.cupola`, its dimensions,
+and the separate chimney count.
+
+**Decision:** Build the small capped drum shown above the right-hand corner
+blockhouse in Kurz & Allison panel 5 (`kurz_allison_1893`; public-domain crop
+`data/sources/assets/prefire_views_kevin_2026_08/p3_1.png`). Its occurrence in
+the 1835 reconstruction is inferred from an 1893 retrospective illustration.
+The source is evidence of appearance, never a coordinate or a metric survey.
+
+**What is invented:** the drum is 1.8 m square, centred on the main pyramid;
+its head stands 1.2 m above that roof's apex, under a 35-degree pyramidal cap
+with 0.12 m eaves. Its skirt intersects the main roof. Three dark vent bands
+on each face represent a ventilated wooden drum; the print does not resolve
+their count or construction. The timber finish and roof covering follow the
+existing archetype palette. These dimensions are starting proportions for
+comparison, not a camera-derived measurement or a completed match.
+
+**The chimney choice:** the earlier reconstructed single chimney stood at
+the same centre. No separate stack is distinguishable on this blockhouse
+in panel 5, so it is omitted rather than moved to an unsupported location.
+This does not prove historical absence or settle a concealed heating arrangement.
+
+**Date boundary:** this is the second fort, rebuilt in 1816 and represented
+at the 1835 scene date. Whistler's statement that first-fort cupolas were not
+yet built in 1808 concerns a different fort at an earlier date; it neither
+prohibits a later inferred presence nor establishes this second-fort cupola.
+
+**What is kept:** the 1830-plan footprint, south-west placement, bearing,
+main wall height, jetty and loopholes. No surveyed coordinate is moved to
+make the retrospective composition fit.
+
+**How to resolve:** refine the group camera, rebake, compare the new silhouette
+against panel 5 and the other dated views, and adjust reconstructed dimensions
+where the pictures support it. T-2388 remains open; no `matches` verdict follows
+from adding this feature.
+
+**Ticket:** T-2388.
+**Recorded:** 2026-10-22.
